# A widget that takes no arguments has one block: a second `fn @Twice:` defines the name
# twice (Jimmy's ruling ZD: "this is a name defined twice"), as a second bare `@Twice:`
# block does (neg clause-widget-without-arguments). The checker passes it today. Expected
# diagnostic derived by hand from the ruling. Written by Claude on the claude-bugs branch;
# subject to change.
emit Ui.*
use Ui.*

@Twice: @unit
fn @Twice:
    Ui.Label($text=$"one")
fn @Twice:
    Ui.Label($text=$"two")

@page: @unit
@page:
    @Twice
